# TODO - C-level source mapping and debugging

## Objective

Generate source maps from Malbolge addresses through lowered IR back to C source
locations. Expose debugging at the C level; keep low-level VM tracing primarily
for implementation and verification.

## Acceptance

- Source maps preserve admitted C file/function/line/IR-region identity
  through lowering and address-sensitive layout with deterministic reverse
  lookup and boundary/error cases. Variable values and high-level stepping
  are reported only when recoverable from verified state/provenance; full C
  variable debugging is not a P3 release requirement.
- Source maps provide deterministic boundaries for an optional annotated
  Malbolge view so generated output can mirror C translation units, functions,
  blocks, and source lines without changing canonical target bytes.
- The stage has deterministic input/output form, rejects malformed or
  unsupported input explicitly, and preserves source/profile provenance needed
  downstream.
- No placeholder, hidden host substitution or undocumented workaround is
  permitted on this TODO's frozen admitted acceptance path. Unsupported or
  untested extensions fail explicitly and do not silently expand that path.
- Evidence is durable enough to move this TODO to `docs/todo/completed/` and
  remove the exact TODO heading without losing unfinished intent.
- A minimal compiled real-C fixture demonstrates correct source-address
  diagnostics through self-modification and relocation. Complete interactive
  source debugger UI, breakpoint protocol and optimizer-aware variable
  reconstruction are not prerequisites of the P3/P5 compiler.
- **Finite acceptance witness:** One real compound C fixture with
  source/function/line mapping through guest addresses, one
  relocated/self-modifying region and one unmappable diagnostic; no interactive
  debugger or arbitrary variable reconstruction.

## Evidence

- Expected durable artifact surface: `compiler/`, `src/`, `tests/compiler/`.
- Required evidence: golden/round-trip or normalized stage fixtures,
  deterministic hashes where promised, and end-to-end lowering regression cases.
- Prerequisite completion evidence: `typed-compiler-ir`,
  `malbolge-layout-and-encoding-backend`.
